eval[0].content: Growth has done more than anything else to reduce absolute poverty, but it does not reduce relative poverty unless the bottom gains faster than the middle. The pattern of growth matters more than its rate. Labour-intensive growth that raises wages at the bottom cuts poverty far more than growth from a mine or an oil field, and the tax revenue growth brings reduces poverty only if it is spent on the poor.
